## 4a24503a Move the waiting update out of updateRoutes, which the stand-down pushed over the gate

The author check on 972ea31c was red on one gate only: crapper counted updateRoutes at CC 20, since it counts the closures
inside a function, and the stand-down had touched it. All 1642 related tests were green there. UpdateWait now holds the update
that waits, its timers and the held turns; the routes keep only what they answer. updateRoutes is CC 1. Nothing changes in
what the routes do, and test/updates.test.ts proves it unchanged.

The flag done in sendWhenIdle goes, since callOff clears waiting in the same step, so the request is no longer the wanted one.

Ruling: split updateRoutes into routes.ts and a new updates/wait.ts, against the brief's "do not reorganise" - why: the gate says every changed function stays under CRAP 10, split first, and the closures are what it counts - cost if wrong: one more file to read; a lane that changes updates/routes.ts must merge with the move.

